---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site';

const updated = '19 October 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy | Lensprout"
  description="Lensprout records, edits and exports on your device. It has no servers and collects no personal data. Here is exactly what the extension stores and why it needs each permission."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-10 pb-16 sm:px-6">
    <header>
      <h1 class="text-4xl leading-tight font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 text-xl leading-relaxed">
        Short version: Lensprout runs entirely on your computer. It has no servers, no accounts and
        no analytics, and it never sends your recordings or any other data anywhere.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 text-sm font-bold">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose mt-10">
      <p>
        This policy covers the Lensprout Chrome extension and this website. "We" means the
        developer of Lensprout.
      </p>

      <h2>What the extension collects</h2>
      <p>
        Lensprout collects nothing for us. We do not receive, sell, share or analyse any data from
        the extension. Everything it creates stays in your browser profile on your device.
      </p>

      <h2>What the extension stores on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Recordings:</strong> the screen, window, audio, microphone and webcam video you
          choose to record.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Input timeline for automatic zoom:</strong> while a recording is running, on web
          pages in Chrome, Lensprout notes pointer positions and clicks, the cursor shape, where the
          text cursor is while you type, and the names of keyboard shortcuts you press (for example
          "Ctrl+C"). It does <strong>not</strong> record the text you type. Password, one-time code
          and payment card fields are skipped entirely.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Projects and settings:</strong> your edits, style presets, recorder preferences,
          theme and font choice.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Exports:</strong> MP4 and GIF files you create, until you download or clear them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data lives in the extension's own storage (IndexedDB, the Origin Private File System
        and <code>chrome.storage.local</code>). Other websites and extensions cannot read it. You can
        delete any recording in the library. Uninstalling the extension or clearing its site data
        removes everything.
      </p>

      <h2>Network access</h2>
      <p>
        The extension makes no network requests to us or to anyone else. Recording, editing and
        exporting all happen locally. Export files are saved only where you choose to download
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>Why the extension asks for each permission</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Screen and window capture</strong> (<code>desktopCapture</code>): to record the
          screen or window you pick in Chrome's picker.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Access to web pages</strong> (<code>http/https</code> hosts, <code>scripting</code>,
          <code>activeTab</code>): to show the countdown on your page and to note clicks and typing
          positions for automatic zoom, only while you record.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tabs and navigation</strong> (<code>tabs</code>, <code>webNavigation</code>): to
          find the page you are recording and keep following it when it navigates.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Display information</strong> (<code>system.display</code>): to line up pointer
          positions with the screen being recorded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Storage</strong> (<code>storage</code>, <code>unlimitedStorage</code>): to keep
          recordings and projects on your device. Videos can be large.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Camera and microphone:</strong> only when you choose a device in the recorder;
          Chrome asks for your permission first.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no analytics, no tracking cookies and no advertising. It is a static site
        hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel may process standard request data such as your
        IP address and browser type to deliver and protect the site; see
        <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Lensprout does not knowingly collect information from anyone, including children.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new "last
        updated" date. Because we collect no data, changes cannot affect data we hold about you.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
